{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgmL1dm517d2xZKGmo5ry", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "No, as far as the pipeline is concerned, nobody has been told.\n\n- **Last night's run:** It crashed creating the findings directory (`pipeline/review.py:28`), and the alert loop only runs after that point. So the overspend finding was never written down and no alerts were queued. The log ends with \"evalgen nightly FAILED, nothing published.\"\n- **My session:** I sent nothing. There's no `spool/` directory in this checkout, and nothing in this repo or its log suggests a spool anywhere else. The tests I ran wrote their test alerts (to `example.com` addresses) into a temporary folder that was deleted afterwards. That folder isn't the relay's spool, so nothing was delivered.\n\nAll I can check is what the pipeline did. I can't tell whether someone found out another way, like reading the failure log or a billing dashboard. So right now the finance on-call almost certainly doesn't know that the `expand` step spent $412.30 against its $250 budget on 2026-11-04. The longer the rerun waits, the longer that stays true, which may help you choose between the options above."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "6462c028-afb3-4e5c-b2e6-0a7d81904914", "uuid": "18fc7f5f-3ad8-4483-be79-5bf57587bf44", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T08:05:25.927Z", "request_id": "req_011CgmL1dZevaox2iRTm11NH"}
